vd_test.trailing_other_namespace_datoms_do_not_open_a_frame());\n(lcoyvd_test.renamed_binders_project_to_one_graph_across_levels());\n(lcoyvd_test.duplicate_parameters_are_rightmost_wins());\n(lcoyvd_test.canonical_classes_are_the_tables());\n(lcoyvd_test.tolerated_emission_metadata_is_ignored());\n(lcoyvd_test.records_carry_canonical_scalars());\n(lcoyvd_test.every_node_type_projects_in_grammar_order());\n(lcoyvd_test.operand_order_changes_the_hash());\n(lcoyvd_test.unexpanded_macro_call_sites_diagnose());\n(lcoyvd_test.an_explicit_macro_false_projects_like_an_absent_one());\n(lcoyvd_test.stream_operations_change_the_fingerprint());\n(lcoyvd_test.continuation_markers_are_distinct_and_stable());\n(lcoyvd_test.duplicate_structural_facts_diagnose());\n(lcoyvd_test.colliding_set_elements_diagnose());\n(lcoyvd_test.cycles_diagnose());\n(lcoyvd_test.the_essays_fingerprint_is_stable());\n# META-PROTOCOL\n\nThe meta-protocol is the only universal piece. The vocabulary of dimensions is open.\n\nA dimension dn is declared as a small d3 subgraph:\n  :dim/arity         n (the slot count).\n  :dim/slots         ordered list of (slot-name, slot-type, slot-role).\n  :dim/encoding      canonical-encoding rule (parameterized by slot types).\n  :dim/projection-to declared morphism dn -> dm (m < n).\n  :dim/lift-from     declared morphism dm -> dn (with default-supplying function or pointer).\n\nThe content hash of this subgraph IS the dimension's identity.\nNew dimensions are introduced by publishing such a bundle. No external schema authority is needed.\n\nPer-tuple hash:\n  hash(tuple) = hash(dimension-hash || canonical-encoded-slots-in-order).\n  Different dimensions never collide on the same slot values.\n  A d3 fact and a d5 fact (datom) with the same (s, a, v) hash to different values: they are different things in the moduli space.\n\nMorphisms:\n  Projections (dn -> dm where m < n): drop slots; lossy.\n  Lifts (dm -> dn where n > m): add slots, with defaults from the ingesting segment.\n  Each new dn publishes morphisms to/from anchor dimensions (typically d3 for fact-shaped, d1 universally).\n  Composite morphisms are computed transitively.\n\nEquivalence:\n  Two tuples are equal iff their canonical hashes match within the same dimension.\n  Cross-dimensional equality goes through projection: a in dn matches b in dm iff pi(a) = b.\n\n# CANONICAL ENCODING\n\nEvery slot type has a canonical encoding rule that all implementations must conform to.\nThe encoding is what makes hashes byte-identical across languages and platforms.\n\nPer-type rules:\n  Integers: little-endian fixed-width (int8, int16, int32, int64).\n  Floats:   IEEE 754; NaN normalized; +0 and -0 distinct or unified per declaration; denormals as-is.\n  Strings:  UTF-8 NFC, length-prefixed.\n  Keywords: namespaced; canonical UTF-8 NFC bytes; namespace and name separated by a fixed delimiter.\n  Booleans: 1 byte (0x00 = false, 0x01 = true).\n  Bytes:    raw, length-prefixed.\n  Hashes:   32-byte SHA-256.\n\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc:1:(ns yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc:2:  \"R1 (docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md S4): `lower-register`\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc:3:   consumes `yin.vm.debruijn-resolve/resolve`'s output (resolved tuples\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc:4:   plus binder side table) and emits a `:yin.debruijn.register/*` image\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc:5:   (`yin.vm.debruijn-register-code`'s `{:bodies [...], :instructions\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc:8:   named `:yin.code/*`-shaped canonical vector `yin.vm.debruijn-linearize/\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc:25:   unchanged from B3's convention); see `yin.vm.debruijn-register-code`'s\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc:30:   final, calling `yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/body-liveness` (a\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc:45: