{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '19,40p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md; sed -n '233,255p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc | sed -n '590,667p'; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest' test/yin/vm/debruijn_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '19,40p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md; sed -n '233,255p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc | sed -n '590,667p'; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest' test/yin/vm/debruijn_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"execution artifact and the sole sharing identity, H. The merged projection is\nan alpha-canonical, lossy historical artifact. It is dormant, has no consumer\nin this design, and is not itself executable.\n\nArchitecture A means lowering from projected records. Architecture B, the\nrecommended architecture, lowers from named datoms and is not the same as A.\nLowering projected records cannot promise named execution semantics because\nprojection deliberately canonicalizes scalar spelling, preserves free names\nonly in canonical form, removes binder names and provenance, and drops\nfront-end `:yin/tail?`. Restricting the input to already-canonical programs,\nweakening continuation guarantees, and treating the records as a cache key\nwould make that path unsound; making them non-identities would make it a poor\nexecutable artifact.\n\nNamed datoms remain the lossless truth. Binder names and provenance are kept\nin the diagnostic side table used by the executable image, while lexical\npositions are derived by `resolve-name`; no second lossless fact structure is\npersisted. This follows the datom.world rule \"derive, don't persist\".\n\nThe executable VM promises equivalence with the named semantic VM only after\nnormalization. Results, effects, streams, cursors, stores, terminal and\nblocked outcomes, and errors must agree. Error comparison uses the message;\ndatoms and reuses only the public `yin.vm.debruijn/resolve-name` helper.\nThat helper compares names exactly, including rightmost-wins duplicate\nparameters, and does not canonicalize values. Projection-only helpers such\nas `index-frame`, `build-node`, and `project-node` are not reused.\nUnexpanded-macro validation remains the named front end's responsibility.\nThe projection is therefore kept, not removed: if it is ever retired, this\npublic helper must first move into the resolver's namespace.\n\n### 3.1 Resolved tuples\n\nThe named datoms are a finite graph, not a tree. `ast->datoms-with-root`\nemits a node carrying a pre-assigned `:eid` exactly once and references it\nfrom every site that names it, for every node type. One source entity can\ntherefore sit under two different lexical contexts, and its resolution is\nthen different at each: the existing projection fixture\n`shared-nodes-resolve-per-their-lexical-context` places one `:variable`\nentity as the body of both `(fn [x] ...)` and `(fn [y] ...)`, bound `[0 0]`\nunder the first and free `x` under the second. Resolution is a fact about\nan occurrence, not about a source entity, so resolved tuples are keyed by\noccurrence. Writing resolution facts onto the shared source entity would\ngive one entity two contradictory fact sets and is not permitted.\n\nAn occurrence is the pair `[source-eid lexical-context]`, where\n   590\t   binds them — (fn [x x] x) resolves to the second x, [0 1]. Returns\n   591\t   {:bound [frame-depth position]} or {:free name} with the symbol\n   592\t   preserved exactly.\"\n   593\t  [stack name]\n   594\t  (let [position-in (fn [frame]\n   595\t                      (first (filter (fn [p] (= name (nth frame p)))\n   596\t                                     (range (dec (count frame)) -1 -1))))\n   597\t        binding (first (keep (fn [depth]\n   598\t                               (when-let [p (position-in (nth stack depth))]\n   599\t                                 [depth p]))\n   600\t                             (range (count stack))))]\n   601\t    (if binding\n   602\t      {:bound binding}\n   603\t      {:free name})))\n   604\t\n   605\t\n   606\t;; =============================================================================\n   607\t;; D1: the projection walk (§2 grammar, §3 scopes, no hashing)\n   608\t;; =============================================================================\n   609\t\n   610\t(declare project-node mint-record)\n   611\t\n   612\t\n   613\t(defn- build-node\n   614\t  \"Build one walked node's resolved semantic node — the §4 projected\n   615\t   slots, children as resolved nodes — recursing over children in the\n   616\t   grammar's fixed order under the scope at each occurrence. Returns\n   617\t   [node child-hashes acc'], child-hashes being {slot h} with an ordered\n   618\t   vector of hashes under :yin.debruijn/operands; `active` is the set of\n   619\t   eids on the current path.\"\n   620\t  [tag index facts scalar eid stack acc active path]\n   621\t  (let [;; each step threads [node child-hashes acc]\n   622\t        child (fn [[node refs acc] slot attr stack]\n   623\t                (let [[n h acc'] (project-node index\n   624\t                                               (child-ref facts attr eid path)\n   625\t                                               stack\n   626\t                                               acc\n   627\t                                               active\n   628\t                                               (conj path attr))]\n   629\t                  [(assoc node slot n) (assoc refs slot h) acc']))\n   630\t        children (fn [[node refs acc] slot attr]\n   631\t                   (let [[ns hs acc']\n   632\t                         (reduce (fn [[ns hs a] ref]\n   633\t                                   (let [[n h a'] (project-node index\n   634\t                                                                ref\n   635\t                                                                stack\n   636\t                                                                a\n   637\t                                                                active\n   638\t                                                                (conj path attr))]\n   639\t                                     [(conj ns n) (conj hs h) a']))\n   640\t                                 [[] [] acc]\n   641\t                                 (child-refs facts attr eid path))]\n   642\t                     [(assoc node slot ns) (assoc refs slot hs) acc']))\n   643\t        leaf (fn [node] [node {} acc])]\n   644\t    (case tag\n   645\t      :literal (leaf {:yin.debruijn/type :literal,\n   646\t                      :yin.debruijn/value (get scalar :yin/value)})\n   647\t      :variable (let [name (get scalar :yin/name)\n   648\t                      resolution (resolve-name stack name)]\n   649\t                  (leaf (if-let [bound (:bound resolution)]\n   650\t                          {:yin.debruijn/type :variable,\n   651\t                           :yin.debruijn/bound bound}\n   652\t                          {:yin.debruijn/type :variable,\n   653\t                           :yin.debruijn/free (:free resolution)})))\n   654\t      :lambda (let [params (get scalar :yin/params)]\n   655\t                (child (leaf (merge {:yin.debruijn/type :lambda,\n   656\t                                     :yin.debruijn/arity (count params)}\n   657\t                                    ;; truthy only: an explicit false and an\n   658\t                                    ;; absent :yin/macro? project identically\n   659\t                                    (when (get scalar :yin/macro?)\n   660\t                                      {:yin.debruijn/macro? (get scalar :yin/macro?)})))\n   661\t                       :yin.debruijn/body\n   662\t                       :yin/body\n   663\t                       (into [params] stack)))\n   664\t      :application (let [operator-eid (child-ref facts :yin/operator eid path)]\n   665\t                     (check-unexpanded index eid operator-eid path)\n   666\t                     (-> (leaf {:yin.debruijn/type :application})\n   667\t                         (child :yin.debruijn/operator :yin/operator stack)\n107:(deftest the-dimension-is-published-with-its-hash-domain\n147:(deftest canonical-classes-are-the-tables\n175:(deftest jvm-out-of-domain-values-diagnose\n186:(deftest a-javascript-number-is-int64-only-when-safe\n199:(deftest the-nfc-seam-composes-on-every-host\n210:(deftest the-node-grammar-is-the-designs-walk-vocabulary\n232:(deftest every-node-type-projects-in-grammar-order\n286:(deftest the-walk-names-children-in-fixed-order\n318:(deftest renamed-binders-project-to-one-graph-at-one-level\n327:(deftest renamed-binders-project-to-one-graph-across-levels\n348:(deftest the-essays-example-resolves-its-binder\n363:(deftest nearest-binder-shadows-with-frame-depth-and-position\n391:(deftest duplicate-parameters-are-rightmost-wins\n405:(deftest free-names-are-preserved-exactly\n417:(deftest shuffled-datom-input-projects-the-same-graph\n426:(deftest transaction-metadata-and-other-namespaces-never-enter-identity\n439:(deftest tolerated-emission-metadata-is-ignored\n446:(deftest the-tail-flag-changes-nothing\n452:(deftest an-explicit-macro-false-projects-like-an-absent-one\n459:(deftest shared-nodes-resolve-per-their-lexical-context\n477:(deftest the-memo-never-affects-output-identity\n496:(deftest adjacent-rooted-graphs-reset-the-fact-index\n512:(deftest a-partial-frame-at-end-of-stream-diagnoses\n522:(deftest trailing-other-namespace-datoms-do-not-open-a-frame\n546:(deftest dangling-references-diagnose\n557:(deftest duplicate-structural-facts-diagnose\n563:(deftest cycles-diagnose\n572:(deftest root-count-diagnoses\n579:(deftest unknown-node-types-diagnose\n586:(deftest unknown-yin-attributes-diagnose-on-walked-nodes\n595:(deftest retracts-diagnose\n602:(deftest unexpanded-macro-call-sites-diagnose\n618:(deftest unsupported-values-diagnose\n627:(deftest malformed-inputs-diagnose\n656:(deftest the-fingerprint-is-the-root-records-hash\n664:(deftest identity-inputs-never-enter-the-fingerprint\n681:(deftest content-changes-change-the-fingerprint\n706:(